  "title": "The knot's signs are a Kasteleyn structure on its minimal surfaces",
  "subject": "The knot's own signs on the least-genus embeddings of the incidence graphs of its three-fold spaces",
  "conclusion": "On every minimal map of every three-fold space with planar glue each face has length 2 mod 4, so the knot's own signs satisfy Kasteleyn's condition; the condition survives every tight-cut splice because exactly three crossing faces form, each joining one face from each side. Non-planar trisum glue behaves the same on all its minimal maps.",
